WEBVTT

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:06.160
I hope so.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:14.580
That's it.

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:19.470
Oh, it's going to be all right.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:23.090
That's it.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.360
That's it. That's it.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.180
It's all right, Albert.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.360
You're going to be OK.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:31.180
I want my daddy!

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:32.720
We'll take you to him.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.220
Easy now. Easy does it. That's it.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.860
Your dad is quite a guy.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.440
I know, Grandpa.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:46.500
He's asleep.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:47.700
He's going to be fine.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.720
How can I thank all of you?

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.080
Thank my son Robbie.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.500
He pulled him out of the water.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:53.720
I'm very grateful, Robbie.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.560
Dad saved him, not me.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.240
I'm so thankful to all of you.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:00.040
So long.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.040
He's a lucky boy.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.540
Well, what do you say we get back to our fishing?

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:08.420
That's a great idea.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:12.420
Uh-oh. It's probably the hospital.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.460
I have to get to a phone.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:19.000
It probably means we can't stay.

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:20.140
That's OK.

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:27.920
One of my patients has a high fever,

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.040
I'm sorry, Robbie.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.100
I guess I ruined your day.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:36.220
You didn't ruin my day, Dad.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:42.840
I understand. I really do.

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.250
Why are you back so early?

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:13.080
Philip had to go back to the hospital.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:14.500
He had an emergency.

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:16.810
Oh, that's too bad, Robbie.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.140
Did it spoil your fun?

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.580
No, Mom. We had a great time.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:25.420
Yeah, we caught lots of them. Look!

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:32.400
They had a special on frozen fish down at the supermarket.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:36.160
Oh, you really had a bad day.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:37.840
We had a good day.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:40.680
Robbie pulled a boy out of the water.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:42.660
And Dad saved his life.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.700
He's a terrific doctor, Mom.

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:46.560
I know.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:02.620
Hello, Dad.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:04.900
What a day!

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.160
How about a cup of coffee, Son?

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:10.180
I'd love a cup of coffee.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:17.840
How was the patient?

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:19.400
She'll be fine.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.500
Was it serious?

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:23.460
No.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:28.480
Until today, I was never really interested in medicine.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.600
Well, it's hard work.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:33.160
Now I know.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.520
I had a good time today, Robbie.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:38.730
Me, too.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:41.400
Why don't we do it again?

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.180
Can we? When?

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:45.960
How about next Saturday?

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.100
Won't you be busy?

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:54.240
Well, do we have a date?

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:55.600
We sure do, Dad.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.080
Grandpa, can you come?

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:00.840
I have other plans, Robbie.

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:05.620
But I think you two can have a good time together without me.

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:11.020
No, Dad, and certainly not without the right magic.
